      "text": "To solve this problem, let's define the two numbers as \\( x \\) and \\( y \\). According to the problem, we have two key pieces of information:\n\n1. The sum of the two numbers is 6.\n2. The difference of their squares is 12.\n\nWe can express these pieces of information as the following equations:\n\\[\nx + y = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nx^2 - y^2 = 12\n\\]\n\nWe recognize that the second equation can be factored using the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\nx^2 - y^2 = (x + y)(x - y)\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the value of \\( x + y \\) from the first equation into the factored form, we get:\n\\[\n(x + y)(x - y) = 12\n\\]\n\\[\n6(x - y) = 12\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\( x - y \\) by dividing both sides of the equation by 6:\n\\[\nx - y = \\frac{12}{6}\n\\]\n\\[\nx - y = 2\n\\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n\\[\nx + y = 6\n\\]\n\\[\nx - y = 2\n\\]\n\nTo find \\( x \\) and \\( y \\), we add these two equations together:\n\\[\n(x + y) + (x - y) = 6 + 2\n\\]\n\\[\n2x = 8\n\\]\n\\[\nx = 4\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( x = 4 \\) back into the first equation to find \\( y \\):\n\\[\n4 + y = 6\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 2\n\\]\n\nThus, the two numbers are \\( x = 4 \\) and \\( y = 2 \\). The positive difference between these two numbers is:\n\\[\nx - y = 4 - 2 = 2\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the positive difference of the two numbers is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
